---
export const prerender = false;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getAllSiteSettings } from '../lib/queries';

const settings = await getAllSiteSettings();
const settingsList = Array.isArray(settings) ? settings : [];
const settingsObj = settingsList.reduce((acc: any, s: any) => { if (s && s.key) acc[s.key] = s.value; return acc; }, {} as Record<string, string>);
const customPrivacy = settingsObj.privacy_custom_text || '';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy - Orandus" description="Privacy policy and data protection guidelines for Orandus.">
  <section class="min-h-screen bg-nitkkr-cream py-12 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto bg-white rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 border border-amber-200/80 shadow-sm space-y-6">
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-nitkkr-dark">🔒 Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Last updated: September 2026</p>
      </div>

      {customPrivacy ? (
        <div class="p-4 bg-amber-50 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-800 leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line">
          {customPrivacy}
        </div>
      ) : null}

      <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">1. What Orandus Is</h2>
          <p>Orandus is a food discovery platform — we help you find food outlets, check menus, see prices, and contact vendors directly. That's it.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">We're <strong>not</strong> a delivery app. We don't cook food, we don't take orders, we don't process payments, and we don't mark up prices. Orandus does not charge commissions on transactions between users and vendors.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">2. What Info We Collect</h2>
          <p>You don't need an account to browse. No sign-up, no login, no tracking pixels following you around.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">The only things we might store:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1">
            <li>Your filter preferences (so you don't have to re-select "High Protein" every time)</li>
            <li>If you dismissed the "Install App" banner</li>
            <li>Your display name and hostel (only if you voluntarily submit a review)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">That's it. We don't collect your personal phone number, email, GPS location, or payment info to browse menus.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">3. Public Student Reviews</h2>
          <p>If you leave a review, it's public. Other students will see your display name, hostel (if you added it), and what you wrote.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Don't include phone numbers or sensitive private information in public reviews.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">4. Review Deletion Requests</h2>
          <p>Need a review removed? Visit our <a href="/contact" class="text-nitkkr-orange font-bold hover:underline">Contact page</a> and let us know. We'll take care of it.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">5. Local Storage (Device-Only)</h2>
          <p>We use your browser's local storage for your saved preferences. It stays on your device. Clearing your browser data removes it completely.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">6. External Links & Communication</h2>
          <p>When you tap a WhatsApp, phone, or other external contact link, you leave Orandus. Your chat or call happens directly on that platform — their privacy policies apply. We don't see your messages, and we don't collect your phone number.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">7. Anonymous Analytics</h2>
          <p>We use privacy-first, cookie-less server metrics to see which pages load, what people search for, or if errors occur. No Google Analytics, no Facebook pixels, no cross-site tracking.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">8. Menu Information & Pricing</h2>
          <p>We work to keep menus, prices, and hours accurate. However, vendors may adjust their prices or availability without notice.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Always double-check with the vendor before you trek across campus or make a purchase. Orandus shows what we know — not a guarantee.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">9. Direct Vendor Interactions</h2>
          <p>You deal directly with the vendor. Price, quality, delivery, refunds, allergies, and hygiene are between you and the food spot. Orandus introduces you to campus spots.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">10. Third-Party Links</h2>
          <p>Maps, Instagram, vendor websites — once you tap out, their rules apply. We don't control them.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">11. No Selling Your Data</h2>
          <p>We don't sell personal info to advertisers. Never have, never will. The data we have exists to make the app work better for you.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">12. Vendor Corrections Welcome</h2>
          <p>Own a food outlet on here? Spot wrong info? <a href="/contact" class="text-nitkkr-orange font-bold hover:underline">Tell us</a>. We'll verify and fix it.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">13. We Might Add Features Later</h2>
          <p>Saved spots, vendor dashboards, ordering tools — if we add stuff that changes how data works, we'll update this policy first.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="font-bold text-base text-slate-900 mb-1">14. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>Questions? Review removal? Data request? <a href="/contact" class="text-nitkkr-orange font-bold hover:underline">Drop us a line</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>